# Home Observatory broker ACL (spec §8.1, §16). Node usernames equal node ids so
# `%u` pins every node to its own topic subtree. Nodes may never publish desired
# config or ACKs, and may never read another node's data.
# Replace "home" if your site id differs.
#
# NOTE: mosquitto `pattern` rules apply to *every* authenticated user, including the
# service accounts below. A service account could therefore publish under
# nodes/<its-own-username>/... . Two layers prevent that from mattering:
#   1. `observatory-server` and `homeassistant` are reserved and rejected as node ids
#      by config validation, and
#   2. the server only accepts frames from node ids registered in the site config,
#      whose topic id matches the frame's envelope id.
# With mosquitto's dynamic-security plugin you can instead bind these patterns to a
# `nodes` role only.

# ---- nodes (pattern rules apply to every authenticated user)
pattern write observatory/v1/home/nodes/%u/telemetry
pattern write observatory/v1/home/nodes/%u/events
pattern write observatory/v1/home/nodes/%u/status
pattern write observatory/v1/home/nodes/%u/capabilities
pattern write observatory/v1/home/nodes/%u/config/reported
pattern write observatory/v1/home/nodes/%u/ota/reported
pattern read  observatory/v1/home/nodes/%u/config/desired
pattern read  observatory/v1/home/nodes/%u/ack
pattern read  observatory/v1/home/nodes/%u/ota/desired

# ---- central server
user observatory-server
topic readwrite observatory/v1/#
topic readwrite homeassistant/#

# ---- Home Assistant (separate credential, sanitized derived state only)
user homeassistant
topic read homeassistant/#
topic read observatory/v1/home/ha/#
topic write homeassistant/status
